From 0a274f9ea6fcab7e5cdcd7ce7ddba24cfa21d3b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-port <linux-port@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:20:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] feat(desktop): install the dsh command on Linux

The macOS shell installs an exact-path command link and Windows uses its own
path manager, but Linux had no host-side implementation at all.

- cli/dsh-linux: POSIX launcher that resolves the packaged resources, reuses
  the Electron binary as the Node runtime, and refuses a transient AppImage
  mount with an actionable message
- command installation/management: Linux branch on ~/.local/bin/dsh with the
  existing ownership semantics (report a conflict, keep a restorable backup,
  never overwrite silently)
- prepare-cli / prepare-command-link: accept Linux and mark the launcher
  executable (the previous code only chmod'ed on macOS)
- tests: exercise the Linux launcher layout on Linux hosts
